---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting Started"
  description="Get started with OMAR - a TUI for managing AI agent organizations"
>
  <h2>What is OMAR?</h2>
  <p>
    OMAR is a TUI for creating powerful agentic organizations. It
    runs on tmux and lets you orchestrate deep hierarchies of parallel AI agents
    from a single terminal.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>tmux 3.0+</strong> &mdash; <code>brew install tmux</code> (macOS) or
      <code>apt install tmux</code> (Debian/Ubuntu)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At least one agent backend:</strong>
      <a
        href="https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/claude-code/overview"
        >Claude Code</a
      >,
      <a href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli">Codex CLI</a>,
      <a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode">Opencode</a>,
      <a href="https://cursor.com/cli">Cursor CLI</a>, or
      <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/gemini-cli">Gemini CLI</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <h3>One-Liner (Recommended)</h3>
  <pre><code>$ curl -fsSL https://omar.tech/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
  <p>
    Works on macOS and Linux. Installs all binaries to <code
      >/usr/local/bin</code
    >.
  </p>

  <h3>Homebrew</h3>
  <pre><code>$ brew install lsk567/omar/omar</code></pre>
  <p>Automatically installs tmux as a dependency.</p>

  <h3>From Source</h3>
  <pre><code>$ git clone https://github.com/lsk567/omar.git
$ cd omar && make install</code></pre>
  <p>Requires Rust 1.70+ and GNU Make.</p>

  <h2>Launch</h2>
  <pre><code>$ omar</code></pre>
  <p>
    This starts the OMAR dashboard with the default agent backend (Claude Code).
    To use a different backend:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Backend</th><th>Command</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td>Claude Code</td><td
          ><code>omar</code> or <code>omar --agent claude</code></td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr><td>Codex CLI</td><td><code>omar --agent codex</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Opencode</td><td><code>omar --agent opencode</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cursor CLI</td><td><code>omar --agent cursor</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Gemini CLI</td><td><code>omar --agent gemini</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Your First Session</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Launch <code>omar</code> &mdash; you'll see the TUI dashboard with your Executive
      Assistant (EA)
    </li>
    <li>
      Copy a test prompt into your EA window:
      <pre><code>Load and run https://github.com/lsk567/omar/blob/main/prompts/tests/project-factory.md</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      Watch agents spawn. Use <strong>&uarr;&darr;&larr;&rarr;</strong> to cycle agents, <strong
        >Tab</strong
      > to drill deeper, <strong>Shift+Tab</strong> to back out
    </li>
    <li>
      To shut down:
      <pre><code>Shutdown the test project and its agents.</code></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Key Bindings</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Key</th><th>Action</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>&uarr;&darr;&larr;&rarr;</code> or <code>j/k</code></td><td
          >Cycle through agents at current level</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>Tab</code></td><td
          >Drill into child agents</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr><td><code>Shift+Tab</code></td><td>Back to parent level</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>Enter</code></td><td>Attach to agent (tmux popup)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>n</code></td><td>Spawn new agent</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>d</code></td><td>Delete agent (with confirmation)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>p</code></td><td>Add project</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>e</code></td><td>Show events</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>r</code></td><td>Refresh status</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>z</code></td><td>Detach from tmux</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>D</code></td><td>Debug console</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>?</code></td><td>Help</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>Q</code></td><td>Quit (with confirmation)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Next Steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/architecture/`}>Architecture & Design</a> &mdash; understand how
